# 5. Confidential / proprietary source material — NEVER commit.
# This remote is a personal GitHub repo. The PDF below is Google Cloud branded
# and marked "Proprietary & Confidential" on 11 of its 22 pages. Ideas and
# public sources may be ported into the deck; the file itself must not be.
alternate_pitch_Oil_&_Gas_Slides_WIP.pdf

# Same rule, same reason. These are Google-internal and partner-confidential
# brand books (go/cloud-icons, FY26 partner guidelines), ~28 MB. The derived
# notes in brand_guidelines/README.md and GEMINI_ENTERPRISE_BRAND_GUIDELINES.md
# are kept; the source PDFs are not.
brand_guidelines/*.pdf

# The pre-commit hook in .githooks/ appends to this file automatically when it
# finds a confidentiality marking in a staged file. See section 7.

# 6. Redundant generated data.
# Superseded by data/personas/ (33 split payloads + index), which is what the
# pages actually load. These two are the old monolithic build, 1.4 MB each,
# regenerated by scripts/extract_persona_research.py whenever needed.
data/persona_research.js
data/persona_research.json

# 7. Auto-added by .githooks/pre-commit
# Anything below this line was staged, found to carry a confidentiality
# marking, unstaged and ignored automatically. Enable the hook with:
#     git config core.hooksPath .githooks
# Override for a single commit with:
#     ALLOW_CONFIDENTIAL=1 git commit ...
